  "notes": "{滅|ほろ}ぶ (godan) and ⟦{滅|ほろ}びる→滅びる：10881_horobiru⟧ (ichidan) mean the same thing. ⟦{滅|ほろ}びる→滅びる：10881_horobiru⟧ is the standard form; {滅|ほろ}ぶ sounds more literary and is common in titles and set phrases. The past tense is {滅|ほろ}んだ (from {滅|ほろ}ぶ) or ⟦{滅|ほろ}びた→滅びる：10881_horobiru⟧ (from ⟦{滅|ほろ}びる→滅びる：10881_horobiru⟧).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive. Transitive pair: ⟦{滅|ほろ}ぼす→滅ぼす：13332_horobosu⟧ (to destroy, to ruin).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{国|くに}→国：02204_kuni⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{滅|ほろ}ぶ: a country falls\n- ⟦{文明|ぶんめい}→文明：03611_bunmei⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{滅|ほろ}ぶ: a civilization perishes\n- ⟦{身|み}→身：01764_mi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{滅|ほろ}ぼす→滅ぼす：13332_horobosu⟧: to ruin oneself (with the transitive)",
